commit 5d6052683c7598ec2477db4793ef2347153f330d
Author: Alexander Zuev <zuev.alexander1@huawei.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 9 09:51:29 2026 +0000

    dcp-gather(npu) D2v3: stream the o_proj replication on the gather side stream
    
    The D1v3 token-sharded rebuild replicates the full o_proj on every
    attention-TP rank (192 MiB bf16 per DSA layer, 14.1 GiB per device for
    78 layers) because each rank must emit the COMPLETE [rows, hidden]
    result for its own tokens. That tax is TP- and context-independent and
    puts the full model over the 64 GB HBM edge (48 GiB sharded weights +
    21.6 GiB D1v3 replicas + KV + HCCL).
    
    Drop the standing replica; assemble the matrix on demand:
    
    - the model runner keeps only this rank's dequantized RowParallel
      shard (24 MiB per layer, 1.9 GiB for 78) and registers it by layer
      id (dsa_cp registry: the side stream prefetches layer L+1 from
      inside layer L's forward, where it only holds layer L's module);
    - the DCP gather side stream all-gathers the shards into a
      double-buffered slot (384 MiB per device), issued on the same
      stream immediately after the same layer's context-KV gather, one
      layer ahead -- the ~2 ms collect hides under the layer's SFA and
      absorb, like the KV gather it rides on. The KV-only ready event is
      recorded before it, so the SFA read does not wait for the weight
      assembly; the o_proj GEMM waits on its own event at the last
      moment;
    - the collect runs on the DCP group (one communicator per stream,
      same as the KV gather); the shards are attention-TP RowParallel,
      so the gather is correct only while both groups are the same
      ranks in the same order (true at TP==DCP) -- checked once, loudly.
    
    Cost: +192 MiB of HCCS per layer per forward on the side stream that
    already moves the context KV. SGLANG_NPU_STREAM_O_PROJ=0 restores the
    D1v3 static replica byte for byte (also the eager no-prefetch path
    gathers synchronously on the compute stream).
    
    Ported onto the combined D2 base: branch_D's D2v3 sits on D2v2 ("shorten
    the gather's AIV episodes"), which combined does not carry. The o_proj
    streaming is independent of that AIV rework, so the side-stream hook is
    placed at the equivalent point in D2's inline _gather_prefix (right after
    the KV ready event), not in D2v2's _dcp_issue_gather_chunks; the rank /
    attn_tp_size attributes used by the collect are the same ones the KV
    gather already relies on.
    
    Source: branch_D 836ac70fc9 (dcp-gather(npu) D2v3).

commit 22ad5f39238aa88c47cb5ace59111b19af327096
Author: Alexander Zuev <zuev.alexander1@huawei.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 9 08:03:19 2026 +0000

    sfa-kv(npu) F: packed int8 SFA latent KV (656 B/row, dequant-on-read) for DCP, gate SGLANG_NPU_SFA_KV_8BIT (default off)
    
    Store the DSA/MLA latent KV as packed 8-bit rows for the DCP serving read --
    the A2/A3 path, where int8 is the latent's only 8-bit dtype (the in-tree FP8
    variant is 950PR-only). Row = latent int8 x512 | rope bf16 x64 | per-128-tile
    fp32 scale x4 = 656 B/token/layer (vs 1152 B bf16, ~x1.76 capacity at fixed
    GiB). The read is the DCP dequant-on-read gather (F1); F2 (paged int8 read)
    is left out.
    
    - SGLANG_NPU_SFA_KV_8BIT (default off): master gate. Requires DCP
      (attn_dcp_size >= 2) -- the serving read is the DCP gather and the paged
      packed read is not wired, so dcp_size 1 is refused at pool init.
    - memory_pool_npu.py: pack (npu_dynamic_quant per 128-tile, dst=store_dtype)
      into the 656 B row; get_mla_kv_buffer dequants on read (both halves
      contiguous -- npu_sparse_flash_attention_lse rejects a non-contiguous
      key_rope); index-K keeps its OWN store dtype (get_index_k_buffer returns it
      raw: viewing it through the latent store_dtype mis-typed the int8 key and
      broke npu_quant_lightning_indexer); set_index_k_buffer writes index_K in
      index_k_store_dtype; DCP extend write owner-filter; index-K int8 + fp16
      scale buffer.
    - kv_cache_configurator.py / pool_configurator.py: NPU pool dim + sizing set
      to the 656 B row under the gate.
    - ascend_backend.py: DCP decode F1 dequant-gather (get_mla_kv_buffer -> TND);
      CP-balance and unsharded paged-read refusals.
    - mla_preprocess.py: refusal for the unsupported combination.
    
    Tests: CPU pack/dequant round-trip (row == 656 B, int8 per-tile bound) and a
    box round-trip (real npu_dynamic_quant int8, DCP owner rule, get_key_buffer
    raw int8, dcp_size 1 -> ValueError).
    
    Source: ported from branch_F opt/sfa-kv-quant (HEAD ead9e9da7a), the FP8
    variant re-targeted to int8 for A2/A3.

